<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Seventeenth Dynasty of Egypt</h1><p class="st-meta">1580 BCE – 1550 BCE (approx.) · capital Thebes</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Theban kings who began the war that drove the Hyksos from Egypt and paved the way for the New Kingdom.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1580 BCE a new line of kings took power at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a>, following the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sixteenth-dynasty-of-egypt">Sixteenth Dynasty of Egypt</a>. At first they acknowledged the overlordship of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/fifteenth-dynasty-of-egypt">Hyksos</a> Fifteenth Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in the north and the power of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kerma">Kerma</a> in the south, and ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-egypt">Upper Egypt</a> from Elephantine to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/abydos">Abydos</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Theban court was modest, its kings buried in small pyramids at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dra-abu-el-naga">Dra Abu el-Naga</a>, but it built up a strong army. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seqenenre-tao">Seqenenre Tao</a> began open war with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/fifteenth-dynasty-of-egypt">Hyksos</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apepi">Apepi</a>, and his mummy shows fatal head wounds from axes. His successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamose">Kamose</a> campaigned north to the walls of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avaris">Avaris</a>, and his stelae at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnak">Karnak</a> record an intercepted letter from Apepi to the ruler of Kush.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmose-i">Ahmose I</a>, probably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamose">Kamose's</a> younger brother, came to the throne around 1550 BCE and completed the war, later taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avaris">Avaris</a> and reuniting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. His reign is counted as the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eighteenth-dynasty-of-egypt">Eighteenth Dynasty</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/egyptian-empire-new-kingdom">Egyptian Empire New Kingdom</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/seventeenth-dynasty-of-egypt.jpg" alt="Seventeenth Dynasty of Egypt" width="320" height="448"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:P1200374_Louvre_roi_Antef_E3019_rw.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1580 BCE – 1550 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century-bce">16th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Thebes</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Seqenenre Tao, Kamose</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Egyptian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Egyptian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Seventeenth Dynasty, Theban Seventeenth Dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1565&amp;focus=seventeenth-dynasty-of-egypt" aria-label="Seventeenth Dynasty of Egypt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5543 1232 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Seventeenth Dynasty of Egypt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5863 1488L5863 1489M5863 1488L5863 1488M5863 1488L5824 1311"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5863 1489h0M5863 1488h0M5824 1311h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5863 1488h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5863 1488h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Thebes. <a href="/atlas?year=-1565&amp;focus=seventeenth-dynasty-of-egypt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
